4530"} "Oliver Klemet"] " (who had already placed seventh in the 400 m freestyle on July 27), with Rasovszky pulling ahead on the final lap to win gold."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The bronze medal went to Hungarian " [:a {:href "/athletes/154561"} "Dávid Betlehem"] ", which was a surprise as, prior to 2024, he had never won a major international individual medal, although he had won the 5 km gold medal a few weeks before the Olympics at the European Championships. Rasovszky and Betlehem’s medals were the first for Hungary in this event at the Olympic Games."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Bib"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {} "Lap 1"] [:th {} "Lap 2"] [:th {} "Lap 3"] [:th {} "Lap 4"] [:th {} "Lap 5"] [:th {} "Lap 6"] [:th {} "Lap 2 Split"] [:th {} "Lap 3 Split"] [:th {} "Lap 4 Split"] [:th {} "Lap 5 Split"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "19"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/134387"} "Kristóf Rasovszky"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HUN.png"}] "HUN"]] [:td {} "1-50:52.7"] [:td {} "17:06.2 (3)"] [:td {} "18:24.5 (2)"] [:td {} "18:38.2 (5)"] [:td {} "18:53.5 (5)"] [:td {} "18:44.2 (7)"] [:td {} "19:06.1 (2)"] [:td {} "35:30.7 (1)"] [:td {} " 54:08.9 (1)"] [:td {} "1-13:02.4 (1)"] [:td {} " 1-31:46.6 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "14"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/154530"} "Oliver Klemet"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "1-50:54.8"] [:td {} "17:07.1 (4)"] [:td {} "18:37.4 (10)"] [:td {} "18:34.2 (2)"] [:td {} "18:49.9 (1)"] [:td {} "18:42.2 (3)"] [:td {